<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CLOUD COVER</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Cloud cover (%, as filed by HRRR): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km TCDC total cloud cover, entire-atmosphere analysis (hourly cycles + 15-min subhourly steps)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 05:00 AM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t09z-tcdc-anl<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (hourly HRRR cycle, 15-min steps)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Cloud_Cover.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
